"F01237"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkImageExecutor.cs"	"55"	"59"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkImageExecutor.public void EvictForColdDecode(string path)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"EvictForColdDecode: evicts the RAM key and the preload-consumed marker, then ClearDisk() which only touches the executor's own scratch _diskCacheDirectory (checked PreviewImageService.ClearDisk uses _diskCacheDirectory), never the user's real cache; called in the untimed prepare step of FirstFrame so the cold decode really comes from source."
"F01238"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkImageExecutor.cs"	"57"	"57"	"SimpleLambdaExpression"	"BenchmarkImageExecutor.lambda in EvictForColdDecode"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Lambda `normalized => _preloadScheduler.RemovePreloadedKeysForPath(normalized)` forwards the normalised key path so a later TryConsumePreloadedKey cannot report a stale preload hit for an evicted path."
"F01239"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkImageExecutor.cs"	"64"	"76"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkImageExecutor.public Task<IDecodedImage> DecodeAsync(string path, CancellationToken token = default)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"DecodeAsync: ThrowIfCancellationRequested before work (cancellation only between decodes, documented); a preload hit is counted only when the RAM cache already held the key AND the scheduler had marked it preloaded, mirroring MainWindow so Preload/WarmNext hit counts are not inflated. Covered by BenchmarkWorkloadRunnerTests.WarmNextWorkloadRecordsPreloadHitAfterWarming."
