"F01245"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkImageExecutor.cs"	"111"	"134"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkImageExecutor.public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"DisposeAsync: cancels the scheduler before awaiting the last preload task (bare catch is intentional so a failed preload cannot fail teardown), disposes the scheduler, flushes persist workers (failure logged), then starts the scratch-dir delete on a background task without awaiting; every executor has its own Guid dir so a lingering prune cannot race the next profile. Not idempotent (second call disposes the scheduler again and replaces TeardownBackgroundTask) but harmless because delete is guarded by Directory.Exists. Covered by BenchmarkImageExecutorTeardownTests.DisposeAsync_DoesNotBlockOnPrune_ButStillCleansUpEventually."
"F01246"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkImageExecutor.cs"	"136"	"156"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkImageExecutor.private async Task DeleteScratchDirectoryAfterPruneAsync()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"DeleteScratchDirectoryAfterPruneAsync: waits up to 2 min for the prune, leaves the dir (logged) if it never settles, deletes only _diskCacheDirectory (own Guid dir under %TEMP%) recursively, all exceptions observed and logged; never touches photo folders. Covered by the teardown test above."
"F01247"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkImageExecutor.cs"	"170"	"183"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkProfileScope.public static IDisposable ApplyLogging(BenchmarkProfile profile, Func<bool> getEnabled, Action<bool> setEnabled, Func<int>? getWriteCount = null)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"ApplyLogging: null-checks all delegates, records previous state before applying DetailedLogging, restore is skipped when getWriteCount changed (user toggled logging in Settings during the run). Covered by BenchmarkTrustTests.ProfileScope_AppliesAndRestoresLogging / ProfileScope_LoggingChangedDuringRun_IsNotOverwritten."
