"F01312"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"53"	"113"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.public static async Task<Func<Task<(bool Correct, ReviewMetricsSnapshot? Metrics)>>> PrepareIterationAsync( BenchmarkImageExecutor executor, string[] files, BenchmarkProfile profile, BenchmarkWorkload workload, int iteration, Random random, IRecycleBin recycleBin, CancellationToken ct)"	"ISSUE"	"PrepareIterationAsync: correct dispatch (not-implemented guard first, FileAction, FirstFrame with untimed cold eviction, Preload/WarmNext single navigation step, otherwise bounded Parallel.ForEachAsync), but with files.Length==0 behaviour is inconsistent: FirstFrame/Preload/WarmNext throw DivideByZero/IndexOutOfRange from SelectIndex while the parallel path builds zero-length selected[] and `results.All` of an empty array returns true, i.e. a Pass with nothing decoded. Both front ends guard empty folders today (BenchmarkWindow files.Length==0, Cli Program.cs), so this is a public-API robustness gap only. See BW-01. Covered partly by BenchmarkWorkloadRunnerTests; no empty-folder test found."
