"F01319"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"115"	"208"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.private static async Task<Func<Task<(bool Correct, ReviewMetricsSnapshot? Metrics)>>> PrepareFileActionAsync( BenchmarkImageExecutor executor, string[] files, BenchmarkProfile profile, int iteration, IRecycleBin recycleBin, CancellationToken ct)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"PrepareFileActionAsync: untimed setup copies the chosen photo into a Guid-named .bin under %TEMP% (File.ReadAllBytesAsync then WriteAllBytesAsync, source opened read-only, never modified); the setup catch calls Cleanup() and rethrows; measure step mutates only temp/moved/copied paths and Cleanup runs in finally; no path ever points into the photo folder or touches the real Recycle Bin unless the opt-in env var is set. Reading the whole source file into memory is acceptable for a benchmark (RAW 100 MB). Covered by BenchmarkWorkloadRunnerTests.FileActionProfilePerformsItsOwnOperation and PrepareIterationAsync_FileAction_ActionRunsOnlyInMeasureStep."
"F01320"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"121"	"126"	"LocalFunctionStatement"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.Cleanup()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Cleanup local function: deletes exactly temp, temp+"".moved"", temp+"".copy"" (all own Guid names), each guarded by File.Exists and a catch limited to IOException/UnauthorizedAccessException so a locked file (decoder still holding it) is left for the OS temp cleaner instead of failing the run; a leftover file is the only consequence."
"F01321"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"138"	"207"	"ParenthesizedLambdaExpression"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.lambda in PrepareFileActionAsync"	"UNREVIEWED"	"Static trace needs controlled evidence; File-action measure lambda: starts the real decode then mutates temp (move+delete / recycleBin.SendToRecycleBin / copy), observes the decode task in every path (no unobserved fault), swallows only IO/UnauthorizedAccess/NotSupported/FileFormat decode failures while rethrowing cancellation, and checks the filesystem contract (source gone for move/delete, present for copy). Suspect only: the scratch file is always named *.bin, so FormatRoutingDecoder routes by extension to the standard decoder; for a RAW source (.cr2/.nef) that decoder throws NotSupported/FileFormat, which is swallowed, so Correct depends only on File.Exists and the profile can Pass without ever exercising a decode. Not proven because BenchmarkImageExecutor uses the default decoder in tests. See BW-04. Covered by BenchmarkWorkloadRunnerTests.FileActionProfilePerformsItsOwnOperation, InterleavedActionProfileCyclesThroughAllThreeOperations."
"F01322"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"213"	"213"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.public static Random CreateSeededRandom(string profileId)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"CreateSeededRandom: new Random(StableHash(profileId)) so each profile replays the same file sequence across processes (string.GetHashCode is randomised per process). Covered by BenchmarkSelectionGoldenTests.CreateSeededRandom_YieldsGoldenSequence."
"F01323"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"215"	"223"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.private static int StableHash(string value)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"StableHash: unchecked 31-multiplier hash over UTF-16 chars, overflow wraps by design, empty string yields 17, deterministic across processes; collisions only mean two profiles share a sequence, harmless. Golden-tested."
