"F01325"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"229"	"229"	"SimpleLambdaExpression"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.lambda in SelectParallelIndices"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Lambda `o => SelectIndex(fileCount, workload, iteration + o, random)`: Enumerable.Select over Range is lazy but materialised by ToArray in the same statement, so Random is consumed in deterministic order (offset 0..count-1), which the golden test relies on."
"F01326"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"232"	"233"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.private static string SelectFile(string[] files, BenchmarkWorkload workload, int iteration, Random random)"	"ISSUE"	"SelectFile: files[SelectIndex(...)] throws IndexOutOfRange/DivideByZero for an empty array (Random.Next(0) returns 0 then files[0] fails); only FirstFrame uses it and callers pre-check emptiness, so latent (BW-01). Covered indirectly by FirstFrame tests; none for empty."
"F01327"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.cs"	"235"	"242"	"MethodDeclaration"	"BenchmarkWorkloadRunner.private static int SelectIndex(int fileCount, BenchmarkWorkload workload, int iteration, Random random)"	"UNREVIEWED"	"Static trace needs controlled evidence; SelectIndex: Random uses random.Next(fileCount); Preload uses iteration*2 % fileCount (iteration*2 cannot overflow for realistic Iterations); `iteration / 2 % fileCount` evaluates as (iteration/2)%fileCount, intended. Suspect: WarmNext alternates iteration 0->0, 1->n-1, 2->1, 3->n-2 so consecutive navigation centres jump across the whole folder instead of stepping forward, and each WarmPreloadAround(center) cancels the previous pass, so a preload hit for the 'next' image is only possible in tiny folders; profile names (WarmNext, fast-balanced, rapid-key-press) suggest sequential next-image navigation. Not proven: intent may be forward+backward coverage and hit rate was not measured. See BW-02. Golden tests cover Random only; WarmNext sequence is not asserted anywhere (BenchmarkStatisticsEdgeTests only checks the images-per-sample table)."
