"F01349"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"107"	"119"	"MethodDeclaration"	"SharedBandwidthLimiter.public void Consume(int bytes)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Consume: ignores bytes<=0, chunks requests larger than one second's budget (bucket is capped at bytesPerSecond) so it cannot spin forever, (int) cast is safe because chunk<=remaining<=int.MaxValue. No dedicated unit test found beyond SlowLinkFileSystemTests/PreloadSlowLinkViewerPriorityTests (Imaging) exercising it indirectly."
"F01350"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"121"	"141"	"MethodDeclaration"	"SharedBandwidthLimiter.private void ConsumeChunk(int bytes)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"ConsumeChunk: refill and take under a lock, sleep outside the lock so concurrent readers share the budget; wait=missing/bytesPerSecond seconds clamped to >=1 ms, `missing` is bounded by bytes<=bps so the wait is <=1 s; loop terminates because refill accumulates. Wall-clock based, see Refill."
"F01351"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"143"	"150"	"MethodDeclaration"	"SharedBandwidthLimiter.private void Refill()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Refill: uses DateTime.UtcNow ticks (not monotonic, a clock step backwards makes elapsed<=0 and only re-bases _lastTicks, a step forward just fills the bucket up to its 1-second cap); _availableBytes starts at 0 and _lastTicks at construction, so the first read after a long idle gets at most one second of burst. Acceptable for a measurement harness; Stopwatch would be stricter."
"F01352"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"156"	"156"	"PropertyDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.CanRead.get"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"ThrottledReadStream.CanRead: forwards inner.CanRead."
"F01353"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"157"	"157"	"PropertyDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.CanSeek.get"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"CanSeek: forwards inner.CanSeek, so callers may Seek on the wrapped stream; bytes consumed by seeks are not metered (reads only)."
"F01354"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"158"	"158"	"PropertyDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.CanWrite.get"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"CanWrite: constant false, consistent with Write throwing NotSupportedException."
"F01355"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"159"	"159"	"PropertyDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.Length.get"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Length: forwards inner.Length; used by pre-read code (new byte[fileStream.Length]), unmetered which is correct because no bytes are transferred."
"F01356"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"160"	"160"	"GetAccessorDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.Position.get"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Position getter: forwards inner.Position."
"F01357"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"160"	"160"	"SetAccessorDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.Position.set"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Position setter: forwards to inner.Position (seek is free, only reads cost tokens)."
"F01358"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"162"	"167"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.public override int Read(byte[] buffer, int offset, int count)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Read(byte[],int,int): reads first then consumes `read` tokens when read>0, so the throttle delays after the data is obtained (average rate is right, first read is not delayed); other paths (ReadByte, CopyTo, ReadAsync) funnel into this override via the Stream base, so no unmetered route exists."
"F01359"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"169"	"174"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.public override int Read(Span<byte> buffer)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Read(Span<byte>): same read-then-consume model; kept as a separate override because Stream.Read(Span) default would rent a buffer and call Read(byte[]) anyway, behaviour identical."
"F01360"	"src/PhotoReview.Benchmarking/SlowLinkFileSystem.cs"	"176"	"176"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ThrottledReadStream.public override long Seek(long offset, SeekOrigin origin)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Seek: forwards to inner.Seek, no metering."
