"F01372"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Abstractions/IDisplayClock.cs"	"38"	"38"	"PropertyDeclaration"	"VBlankEstimator.Count.get"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"VBlankEstimator.Count.get returns _count (0..Capacity=32); single-threaded by contract (WindowsDisplayClock owns one estimator per monitor thread). Asserted indirectly by FewerThanTheMinimumSamples_GiveNoTiming."
"F01373"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Abstractions/IDisplayClock.cs"	"40"	"45"	"MethodDeclaration"	"VBlankEstimator.public void Reset()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Reset sets _count=0,_next=0,Current=null; stale _samples are never read because Sample(index) is bounded by _count. Verified the ring arithmetic after Reset and that DropSamplesBeforeARateChange re-seeds through the same fields. Covered by ARefreshRateChange_IsFollowedWithinAFewRefreshes."
"F01374"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Abstractions/IDisplayClock.cs"	"48"	"56"	"MethodDeclaration"	"VBlankEstimator.public void Add(long timestamp)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Add ignores timestamp <= previous sample (NonIncreasingTimestamps_AreIgnored), appends in the 32-slot ring, then runs DropSamplesBeforeARateChange and Compute. Ring index math checked for wrap-around. Transient mis-estimate with few samples originates in Compute (see F01346), not here."
"F01375"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Abstractions/IDisplayClock.cs"	"61"	"91"	"MethodDeclaration"	"VBlankEstimator.private DisplayTiming? Compute()"	"ISSUE"	"Compute uses the lower quartile of the intervals as the one-refresh baseline; with the minimum 4 samples (3 intervals) that is the minimum interval, so a single late wake-up makes it far below one refresh and every other interval is rounded to 2 refreshes. Reproduced: 60 Hz vblanks with one sample 0.4 refresh late, 4 samples -> RefreshPeriod 100000 ticks vs true 166666 (-40 percent). Self-heals as the 32-sample window fills, so transient (Predict kinetic glide). See finding N-core-io-F01."
"F01376"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Abstractions/IDisplayClock.cs"	"93"	"93"	"MethodDeclaration"	"VBlankEstimator.private long Sample(int index)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Sample(index) = _samples[(_next - _count + index + Capacity) % Capacity]: oldest-first mapping verified for _count < Capacity and full ring; always non-negative because _count <= Capacity."
"F01377"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Abstractions/IDisplayClock.cs"	"99"	"122"	"MethodDeclaration"	"VBlankEstimator.private void DropSamplesBeforeARateChange()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Checked guard _count >= Recent + MinSamples (8) so olderIntervals >= 3 (no divide by zero), the 0.15*nearest tolerance, and the Reset-and-reseed of the last 5 samples (count 5 >= MinSamples, Compute recomputed by Add afterwards). Covered by AnIntegerRatioRateChange_IsFollowedWithinTheSampleWindow."
