"F01904"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedOpenCoalescer.cs"	"23"	"29"	"ConstructorDeclaration"	"ForwardedOpenCoalescer.public ForwardedOpenCoalescer(Action<string?> open, TimeSpan window, ILog? log = null, Func<TimeSpan, CancellationToken, Task>? delay = null)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Null open rejected, window stored as-is (a negative/zero window just makes Task.Delay throw or complete, which FlushAfterWindowAsync handles), log defaults to NullLog. Tests: ForwardingCoreTests, Coalescer_WindowDelayFails_IsLoggedAndTheOpenStillHappens."
"F01905"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedOpenCoalescer.cs"	"31"	"47"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedOpenCoalescer.public void Submit(IReadOnlyList<string> paths)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Under _gate: ignored after Dispose; while a window is pending the first non-null path wins (_first ??= first), a path-less request still triggers one open; new window started outside the lock. Tests: Coalescer_BurstOfLaunches_OpensFirstPathOnce, _SeparateBursts_AreSeparateOpens, _Submit_DoesNotRunOrWaitForTheOpenCallback."
"F01906"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedOpenCoalescer.cs"	"49"	"73"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedOpenCoalescer.private async Task FlushAfterWindowAsync(CancellationToken token)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"OperationCanceledException (Dispose) exits without opening; any other delay failure is logged and the open still happens; _pending reset under the lock before _open so a Submit during the open starts a new window; _open exceptions logged. Race: Dispose between the lock and _open can still fire one open (harmless, App posts to a closing UI). Tests: Coalescer_Dispose_CancelsPendingOpen, Coalescer_OpenCallbackThrows_IsLoggedAndTheNextSubmitStillWorks."
"F01907"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedOpenCoalescer.cs"	"75"	"79"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedOpenCoalescer.public void Dispose()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Sets _disposed under the lock then cancels the CTS (CTS itself is not disposed, no timers attached so nothing leaks). Idempotent. Test: Coalescer_Dispose_CancelsPendingOpen."
"F01908"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedPathProtocol.cs"	"18"	"34"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedPathProtocol.public static byte[] Encode(IReadOnlyList<string> paths)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Checked: count > 16, any path failing IsAcceptablePath (shared contract with the decoder), strict UTF-8 (lone surrogates rejected earlier), total size cap 64 KiB. A null element would throw NullReferenceException instead of ArgumentException (contract violation; callers filter with File.Exists). Tests: Encode_ExactlyMaxPaths..., Protocol_Encode_RejectsWhatDecodeWouldReject, Encode_PathWithLoneSurrogate_ThrowsArgumentException."
"F01909"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedPathProtocol.cs"	"37"	"38"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedPathProtocol.public static bool IsComplete(ReadOnlySpan<byte> message)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"True only for length >= 2 ending in two LF bytes; header-only message ""H\n\n"" is complete; a path list cannot contain an empty line so the terminator is unambiguous. Test: IsComplete_OnlyAMessageEndingWithAnEmptyLineIsComplete."
"F01910"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedPathProtocol.cs"	"41"	"61"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedPathProtocol.public static bool TryDecode(ReadOnlySpan<byte> message, Func<string, bool> pathExists, out IReadOnlyList<string> paths)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Untrusted-input parser: size cap, terminator, strict UTF-8 (BOM and invalid bytes rejected), header, <= 16 paths, per-path shape plus pathExists; CRLF rejected through IsControl; any failure returns false with paths=[]. pathExists is called on attacker-chosen strings (UNC could trigger an SMB lookup) but the pipe is CurrentUserOnly. Tests: ForwardedPathProtocolLimitTests (18), Protocol_RejectsHostilePrefixes_EvenIfExists."
"F01911"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedPathProtocol.cs"	"63"	"76"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedPathProtocol.private static bool IsAcceptablePath(string p)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Checked: empty/over-long, control chars, unpaired surrogates, device/extended prefixes in all separator spellings (\\?\, //?/, \??\, \\.\), "".."" segments, IsPathFullyQualified. ""..."" segments are not parent traversal on Windows (verified Path.GetFullPath keeps them). Pattern precedence (p[2] is ? or .) parses as intended. Tests: Path_DeviceOrExtendedNamespace_IsRejectedByEncodeAndDecode, Path_TwoSeparators_NeverCrashesTheShapeCheck."
"F01912"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedPathProtocol.cs"	"78"	"78"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedPathProtocol.private static bool IsSep(char c)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Trivial separator predicate for \ and /."
"F01913"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/ForwardedPathProtocol.cs"	"80"	"88"	"MethodDeclaration"	"ForwardedPathProtocol.private static bool IsWellFormedUtf16(string p)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Rune.DecodeFromUtf16 loop with OperationStatus.Done; consumed advances correctly for pairs; invalid lone high/low surrogate returns false. Tests: Encode_ValidSurrogatePair_RoundTrips, Encode_PathWithLoneSurrogate_ThrowsArgumentException."
"F01914"	"src/PhotoReview.Core/Instance/SecondInstanceHandoff.cs"	"12"	"30"	"MethodDeclaration"	"SecondInstanceHandoff.public static async Task<bool> TryForwardAsync( IInstanceForwardClient client, IReadOnlyList<string> existingPaths, TimeSpan timeout, ILog? log = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Non-cancellation client exceptions are swallowed into false (caller falls back to opening locally); OCE rethrown (the shipped client maps its own timeout to Unknown/NoInstance, so only caller cancellation escapes); Delivered/Unknown -> true per Q-R12 (accepted trade-off). Null existingPaths would NRE only after a successful send (callers pass a list). Tests: Handoff_ExitsOnlyWhenTheOwnerTookOrLikelyTookTheRequest, TryForward_*."
