"F03034"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"89"	"113"	"MethodDeclaration"	"PerfRules.public static RuleResult EvaluateRUi(RulesConfig cfg, IReadOnlyList<NavRecord> ramHitNavs, double ramHitFinalP95, double? frameTimeP95Ms)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"EvaluateRUi: share of (t_input+t_assign+t_render) in final visual time (missing parts count as 0), RamHit P95 and frame-time P95 each tested against thresholds; returns N/A only when all three inputs are absent, otherwise OR of the three; NaN ramHitFinalP95 is guarded explicitly before comparison; nested Invariant formatting is redundant but correct. Covered by RUiTriggersOnHighUiShareOrHighRamHitP95AndIsNotTriggeredOtherwise and RUiTriggersOnHighFrameTimeAlone."
"F03035"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"95"	"95"	"SimpleLambdaExpression"	"PerfRules.lambda in EvaluateRUi"	"UNREVIEWED"	""
"F03036"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"98"	"98"	"SimpleLambdaExpression"	"PerfRules.lambda in EvaluateRUi"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Lambda `n => ((TInputMs ?? 0)+(TAssignMs ?? 0)+(TRenderMs ?? 0)) / n.FinalVisualMs!.Value`: divisor >0 by the Where; TInputMs measured from the key press is part of FinalVisualMs because t0 is the matched KeyInput, so the share is internally consistent."
"F03037"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"118"	"131"	"MethodDeclaration"	"PerfRules.public static RuleResult EvaluateRPre(RulesConfig cfg, double ramHitFinalP95, double nonRamHitSharePct, bool isBurstScenario)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"EvaluateRPre: N/A when there is no RamHit P95; otherwise triggered if RamHit P95 <= ramHitP95MaxMs and the non-RamHit share >= threshold (S3/S4 default 30, S2 default 10 percent); NaN nonRamHitSharePct yields false (comparison with NaN), which cannot happen once a RamHit P95 exists. Covered by RPreTriggersOnFastRamHitWithLowCoverageAndIsNotTriggeredWithGoodCoverage."
"F03038"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"136"	"147"	"MethodDeclaration"	"PerfRules.public static RuleResult EvaluateRCont(RulesConfig cfg, double? decodeMsLowWorkers, double? decodeMsHighWorkers, int? lowWorkers, int? highWorkers)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"EvaluateRCont: N/A when either decode average is missing or the two worker counts are equal (including both null); ratio=high/max(low,0.0001) so a zero-ms low-worker average cannot divide by zero (it yields a huge ratio, which is arguably correct); default factor 1.3; invariant formatting of nullable doubles with F1 works. Covered by RContTriggersOnDecodeSlowdownAndIsNotTriggeredWhenStable and RContIsNotApplicableWithoutTwoDistinctWorkerRuns."
"F03039"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"150"	"161"	"MethodDeclaration"	"PerfRules.public static RuleResult EvaluateRThread(RulesConfig cfg, int dispatcherLongOpCount, double? tInputP95Ms)"	"UNREVIEWED"	"Static trace needs controlled evidence; EvaluateRThread: triggers when dispatcherLongOpCount>0 OR t_input P95>inputP95Ms (default 16), N/A only if there is no long op and no t_input. The XML doc says 'repeated DispatcherLongOp during S2/S3', but a single long op in any scenario (the caller already applied the ms threshold) flags the group, and there is no configurable count threshold, so one stray 17 ms dispatcher op marks R-THREAD true. Possibly intentional (D11 spec not available in the repo anymore) so not proven wrong. See PA-03. Covered by RThreadTriggersOnDispatcherLongOpsOrHighInputP95AndIsNotTriggeredOtherwise (asserts counts 3 and 0 only; a single long op is untested)."
"F03040"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"164"	"170"	"MethodDeclaration"	"PerfRules.public static RuleResult EvaluateRGc(RulesConfig cfg, double? gcTimePercent)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"EvaluateRGc: null gcTimePercent gives N/A, else >= gcTimePct (default 10); the value comes from process.json unvalidated (negative or above 100 accepted) which only affects a diagnostic flag. Covered by RGcTriggersAboveThresholdAndIsNotTriggeredBelow."
"F03041"	"src/PhotoReview.PerfAnalysis/PerfAnalyzeRules.cs"	"175"	"188"	"MethodDeclaration"	"PerfRules.public static RuleResult EvaluateRDisk(RulesConfig cfg, IReadOnlyList<NavRecord> diskCacheHitNavs, IReadOnlyList<NavRecord> sourceMissNavs)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"EvaluateRDisk: compares avg t_disk of DiskCacheHit navs with avg (t_read ?? 0)+t_decode of SourceMiss navs times a factor (default 1.0); N/A unless both sets are non-empty so Average never runs on empty; the read+decode sum is biased low under PA-01 because decode already had the read removed. Covered by RDiskTriggersWhenDiskCacheIsNoFasterThanReDecodingAndIsNotTriggeredOtherwise."
