"F03196"	"src/PhotoReview.Platform.Windows/WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.cs"	"30"	"32"	"MethodDeclaration"	"WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.internal string NameFor(string operationId)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Name is Local\<prefix>_LiveOp_<SHA-256 hex of liveop|SID|id>: fixed length, no illegal kernel-name characters whatever the journal Id holds, per user. A very long prefix could exceed the 260-char object-name limit, which Begin/IsLive convert via ArgumentException handling. Test: NameFor_DistinctPerIdAndPrefix."
"F03197"	"src/PhotoReview.Platform.Windows/WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.cs"	"34"	"47"	"MethodDeclaration"	"WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.public IDisposable Begin(string operationId)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Creates a manual-reset event (no thread affinity, so released from any pool thread) and ignores createdNew deliberately, so two holders of one Id share the name until both dispose; failures (IOException, UnauthorizedAccess, name taken by another object type, bad name) log and return the NoMarker singleton, matching the documented 'never fail the file action for its marker' contract (accepted trade-off, Q-R27 / ILiveOperationRegistry). Tests: Begin_SameIdTwice_LiveUntilLastHolderReleases, Begin_NameTakenByMutex_ReturnsNoMarkerAndLogs, Begin_OddIds_SanitisedAndWork."
"F03198"	"src/PhotoReview.Platform.Windows/WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.cs"	"49"	"67"	"MethodDeclaration"	"WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.public bool IsLive(string operationId)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"TryOpenExisting then immediate Dispose of the probe handle (no leak); UnauthorizedAccessException is treated as live (an elevated owner's event), other IO/argument failures log and answer not-live, which equals pre-Q-R27 reconcile behaviour and is the accepted degradation per ILiveOperationRegistry.cs docs. Test: Begin_VisibleToSecondRegistry_UntilDisposed."
"F03199"	"src/PhotoReview.Platform.Windows/WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.cs"	"73"	"73"	"MethodDeclaration"	"WindowsLiveOperationRegistry.NoMarker.public void Dispose()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Intentional no-op for the shared NoMarker instance; safe to Dispose any number of times or concurrently."
